1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:02,320
Looks like your bad luck
finally wore off.

2
00:00:02,670 --> 00:00:04,000
I'm the one stuck with it now.

3
00:00:04,050 --> 00:00:07,430
I told you already.
You are meant to live as one.

4
00:00:07,710 --> 00:00:10,180
The heaven and earth
do not acknowledge your love.

5
00:00:10,270 --> 00:00:11,630
You're here early...

6
00:00:16,070 --> 00:00:19,030
If you want to keep staying at my place,
you're welcome to.

7
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:20,230
I'd rather not.

8
00:00:20,730 --> 00:00:22,930
I don't want to be a third wheel to you.

9
00:00:23,170 --> 00:00:24,110
For now,

10
00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:27,020
I'll stay with Nadol.

11
00:00:36,980 --> 00:00:37,780
Oh?

12
00:00:38,970 --> 00:00:39,770
Hey!

13
00:00:41,690 --> 00:00:42,880
Come on, Hunglay.

14
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:50,640
Jeez, what's wrong with you
all of a sudden?

15
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:54,680
Is the spark plug acting up?

16
00:01:00,090 --> 00:01:01,310
I already told you

17
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:03,300
that you can still stay at my place.

18
00:01:04,390 --> 00:01:05,530
I'd rather not.

19
00:01:06,210 --> 00:01:08,220
The couch in Nadol's room
is perfectly fine.

20
00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:10,780
You'll end up with a sore back
if you sleep on a couch.

21
00:01:11,810 --> 00:01:12,980
My back is doing alright.

22
00:01:13,860 --> 00:01:15,160
I'm not as old as you are.

23
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:17,920
According to our contract,

24
00:01:18,590 --> 00:01:20,320
you're supposed to stay at my house.

25
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:22,400
Do you even remember what's in it?

26
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:25,400
Our roles as husbands, you know.

27
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:27,900
You're funny, Inspector.

28
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:30,080
You keep reminding me
about the contract.

29
00:01:31,210 --> 00:01:32,710
What about the promise you made?

30
00:01:33,220 --> 00:01:35,070
You said you'd be a faithful husband.

31
00:01:36,820 --> 00:01:37,950
Do you remember that?

32
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:39,820
I just want you to have a good life,

33
00:01:40,160 --> 00:01:41,770
like I promised your mom.

34
00:01:41,910 --> 00:01:43,330
I'm doing just fine right now.

35
00:01:43,740 --> 00:01:45,240
It's you changing your mind all the time

36
00:01:45,260 --> 00:01:46,380
that's making things difficult.

37
00:01:47,650 --> 00:01:49,170
You might want me around today,

38
00:01:50,030 --> 00:01:52,840
but you might push me away tomorrow.

39
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:55,930
What exactly do you want?

40
00:02:07,450 --> 00:02:09,650
Can I give you
a piece of advice, Inspector?

41
00:02:11,170 --> 00:02:14,730
There are psychiatrists
here in Chiang Mai.

42
00:02:16,380 --> 00:02:18,240
I think you should go see one.

43
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:21,080
They might know
why you keep changing your mind.

44
00:02:38,230 --> 00:02:39,520
No, thanks.

45
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:41,400
Come on.

46
00:02:57,860 --> 00:02:59,240
It's started now, so get off.

47
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:39,140
(Yin as Theartha)

48
00:03:44,070 --> 00:03:46,800
(War as Mungkorn)

49
00:03:50,940 --> 00:03:53,290
(Shane as Phuwin)

50
00:03:53,720 --> 00:03:56,760
(Boss as Lukplub)

51
00:03:59,140 --> 00:04:00,870
(Kit as Kanin)

52
00:04:01,130 --> 00:04:03,080
(Tang as Nadol)

53
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:11,800
(Tae as Saming)

54
00:04:56,620 --> 00:04:57,460
Mungkorn.

55
00:04:58,120 --> 00:04:59,010
Lady Pharada?

56
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:00,940
Hello.

57
00:05:02,180 --> 00:05:03,480
Is something the matter?

58
00:05:03,780 --> 00:05:04,690
Yes, of course.

59
00:05:05,250 --> 00:05:06,820
I'm here to bring you back home.

60
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:09,320
Thear told me
you haven't been home for two days.

61
00:05:09,640 --> 00:05:10,600
What happened?

62
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:14,790
It's nothing.

63
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:18,850
I just moved back to where I belong.

64
00:05:19,880 --> 00:05:23,100
The police flats
are the right place for me.

65
00:05:24,530 --> 00:05:27,750
A junior officer shouldn't be staying
at his superior's house.

66
00:05:30,820 --> 00:05:31,690
Mungkorn,

67
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:35,170
I care about you like you're my own son.

68
00:05:35,990 --> 00:05:37,320
Tell me the truth.

69
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:39,840
You're not coming home...

70
00:05:40,380 --> 00:05:42,350
because of Thear and Belle, right?

71
00:05:47,340 --> 00:05:49,480
Do you actually
have feelings for my son?

72
00:05:53,490 --> 00:05:55,620
If you tell me that you don't,

73
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:58,320
I'll let you stay here.

74
00:06:01,020 --> 00:06:02,800
But if the truth is...

75
00:06:03,440 --> 00:06:05,240
you do have feelings for him...

76
00:06:09,040 --> 00:06:11,100
you have to be honest with me, dear.

77
00:06:20,820 --> 00:06:21,620
I do.

78
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:24,620
I think I'm in love
with Inspector Thear.

79
00:06:24,640 --> 00:06:26,000
Then take him back!

80
00:06:26,620 --> 00:06:28,730
Stop acting
like you're his second choice.

81
00:06:28,780 --> 00:06:29,980
You're his only choice.

82
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:30,880
Why would you let her win?

83
00:06:30,900 --> 00:06:35,200
You are his legally wedded spouse
in every sense.

84
00:06:35,340 --> 00:06:37,240
So, what should I do?

85
00:06:37,780 --> 00:06:40,380
Their old spark is burning so brightly.

86
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:43,090
I'll teach you.

87
00:06:43,250 --> 00:06:47,180
Believe it or not,
I'm the president of the Wives Club.

88
00:06:50,110 --> 00:06:50,910
Alright.

89
00:06:51,230 --> 00:06:52,610
It's time to call him yours

90
00:06:52,630 --> 00:06:54,270
and take him back.

91
00:07:06,950 --> 00:07:09,080
When are you heading back to the States?

92
00:07:09,420 --> 00:07:11,080
Probably in a week or two.

93
00:07:11,420 --> 00:07:13,430
Once you've got everything sorted out,

94
00:07:13,530 --> 00:07:14,920
it'll probably be just about time.

95
00:07:17,820 --> 00:07:19,100
Just let me know, then.

96
00:07:19,130 --> 00:07:21,820
In the meantime, make yourself at home.

97
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:30,360
Who's that?

98
00:07:49,160 --> 00:07:50,330
Oh, honey?

99
00:07:50,640 --> 00:07:51,580
Belle?

100
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:53,720
You're back?

101
00:07:54,820 --> 00:07:56,100
Wanna swim with me?

102
00:07:56,180 --> 00:07:57,060
I'm good.

103
00:07:57,200 --> 00:08:00,400
I didn't bring a swimsuit with me.

104
00:08:01,990 --> 00:08:03,640
What about you, honey?

105
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:07,460
Aren't you going to join me?

106
00:08:08,490 --> 00:08:10,760
I thought you weren't coming home.

107
00:08:11,420 --> 00:08:13,240
I wasn't going to,

108
00:08:14,180 --> 00:08:16,200
but like you said, honey...

109
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:19,140
I have to be here to take care of you.

110
00:08:19,880 --> 00:08:21,640
After all,
that's what a husband should do.

111
00:08:22,220 --> 00:08:23,680
Having someone else do it...

112
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:25,540
wouldn't be right.

113
00:08:26,640 --> 00:08:27,950
Don't you agree, Belle?

114
00:08:29,950 --> 00:08:30,750
Yeah.

115
00:08:35,040 --> 00:08:37,620
Are you really not going to join me?

116
00:08:50,940 --> 00:08:52,200
It's hot today.

117
00:08:54,190 --> 00:08:55,730
Should we do something "cool" together?

118
00:08:57,250 --> 00:08:58,120
I'm good.

119
00:08:58,630 --> 00:09:01,090
I'm not in the mood for a swim.

120
00:09:01,670 --> 00:09:03,370
Then what are you in the mood for?

121
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:05,140
I can join you.

122
00:09:06,660 --> 00:09:09,260
I'm pretty tired today.
I just want to rest.

123
00:09:09,910 --> 00:09:11,500
Let's go, Belle.

124
00:09:27,570 --> 00:09:29,130
How is it going, Mungkorn?

125
00:09:29,570 --> 00:09:31,470
They went up to Belle's room together.

126
00:09:32,470 --> 00:09:33,490
What are they doing in there?

127
00:09:34,270 --> 00:09:36,510
I don't know.
They were holding hands, too.

128
00:09:36,840 --> 00:09:37,680
Hey!

129
00:09:37,890 --> 00:09:39,780
Don't you want to find out?

130
00:09:40,300 --> 00:09:41,260
I do.

131
00:09:41,290 --> 00:09:42,620
Then you have to find out.

132
00:09:43,230 --> 00:09:44,780
What do you want me to do?

133
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:51,920
Khaopuk, how is a nosy maid
supposed to act?

134
00:09:53,620 --> 00:09:55,120
When we wanna know something,

135
00:09:55,140 --> 00:09:57,320
we'll pry until we find out.

136
00:09:57,640 --> 00:10:00,050
We have every right to know the truth.

137
00:10:05,250 --> 00:10:06,450
Are we really doing this?

138
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:08,390
Well, if you're curious,
you've got to know.

139
00:10:08,420 --> 00:10:11,190
Remember, she thinks it's special,
but it's all reused. Go!

140
00:10:11,610 --> 00:10:12,680
- Good luck.
- Go on, dear.

141
00:10:14,470 --> 00:10:15,260
Go, go!

142
00:10:19,410 --> 00:10:21,430
- Whoa, it's high!
- Just go!

143
00:10:21,680 --> 00:10:22,970
Good luck, Mr. Mungkorn.

144
00:10:23,830 --> 00:10:25,820
Make sure you eavesdrop successfully!

145
00:10:25,850 --> 00:10:27,690
Thanks for the support, everyone.

146
00:10:43,090 --> 00:10:45,190
How's it going? Are they doing it?

147
00:10:45,420 --> 00:10:46,450
Puk, be quiet.

148
00:10:47,200 --> 00:10:48,090
You're being too loud.

149
00:10:59,990 --> 00:11:01,360
What are you doing up here?

150
00:11:04,270 --> 00:11:05,080
Whoops, run!

151
00:11:05,100 --> 00:11:05,970
Go!

152
00:11:10,890 --> 00:11:11,760
Well...

153
00:11:12,050 --> 00:11:14,530
An injured bird
got stuck on this balcony,

154
00:11:15,120 --> 00:11:16,200
so I came up to help it.

155
00:11:17,300 --> 00:11:18,550
Then it flew away.

156
00:11:19,070 --> 00:11:20,760
I guess it's not hurt anymore.

157
00:11:21,230 --> 00:11:22,920
Seems like
I'm the only one who still is.

158
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:25,230
Oh...

159
00:11:25,850 --> 00:11:27,370
So you're not afraid of heights anymore?

160
00:11:28,500 --> 00:11:29,660
Not anymore.

161
00:11:30,220 --> 00:11:31,790
You have to face it
until you're used to it.

162
00:11:37,630 --> 00:11:40,980
Well, if I see the bird,
I'll catch it for you.

163
00:11:41,550 --> 00:11:43,130
You're such a kind person.

164
00:11:44,270 --> 00:11:45,390
Not really.

165
00:11:46,850 --> 00:11:48,970
When I see someone in trouble,
I always help them.

166
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:52,870
But somehow, people never see my worth.

167
00:11:53,810 --> 00:11:55,510
They just see me as a placeholder.

168
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:08,020
Hey!

169
00:12:08,510 --> 00:12:10,500
You're going down that way?
Isn't it dangerous?

170
00:12:20,660 --> 00:12:22,350
Please allow me to get out of your way.

171
00:12:49,490 --> 00:12:50,560
Hey, Mungkorn.

172
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:53,200
Why are you pressing up against me?

173
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:54,460
Go back to your side.

174
00:12:56,560 --> 00:12:58,090
But I'm cold.

175
00:13:00,220 --> 00:13:03,700
Cuddling my husband
is warmer than using a blanket.

176
00:13:03,970 --> 00:13:07,370
If you're cold, just turn up the AC.

177
00:13:08,010 --> 00:13:09,000
I don't want to.

178
00:13:10,390 --> 00:13:12,800
I'd rather do something
with my husband...

179
00:13:13,410 --> 00:13:15,240
to get warmer.

180
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:46,180
Wait.

181
00:13:46,720 --> 00:13:47,830
I'm burning up.

182
00:13:48,440 --> 00:13:49,500
I'll sleep outside.

183
00:13:59,210 --> 00:14:00,520
Mungkorn,

184
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:02,070
how was last night?

185
00:14:02,100 --> 00:14:04,250
Tell me something good.

186
00:14:04,280 --> 00:14:08,040
Did you two get intimate
under the covers?

187
00:14:09,530 --> 00:14:11,010
We didn't do anything at all.

188
00:14:11,040 --> 00:14:12,000
Oh?

189
00:14:12,020 --> 00:14:14,000
He wouldn't even let me
sleep next to him.

190
00:14:15,210 --> 00:14:16,580
I'm serious.

191
00:14:16,880 --> 00:14:18,610
No matter how much I try to tempt him,

192
00:14:20,140 --> 00:14:22,110
it doesn't work if he doesn't want it.

193
00:14:22,740 --> 00:14:25,690
Maybe you weren't sexy enough?

194
00:14:26,450 --> 00:14:27,510
It's possible, My Lady.

195
00:14:28,100 --> 00:14:32,330
Come on, there are still
a hundred more ways.

196
00:14:34,780 --> 00:14:36,170
Thear, gosh...

197
00:14:37,560 --> 00:14:39,790
I guess I'll have to
play hardball with him.

198
00:14:43,810 --> 00:14:44,760
Thear!

199
00:14:45,300 --> 00:14:46,420
Where are you off to?

200
00:14:49,920 --> 00:14:50,980
Oh...

201
00:14:51,550 --> 00:14:54,620
I'm taking Belle to a waterfall.

202
00:14:55,260 --> 00:14:57,000
We're going camping for a night.

203
00:14:59,230 --> 00:15:00,900
Oh, that's perfect!

204
00:15:01,120 --> 00:15:04,090
Mungkorn is a real nature lover.

205
00:15:04,120 --> 00:15:06,930
He loves the planet,
the mountains, and everything.

206
00:15:06,950 --> 00:15:10,190
He wants to go
to the waterfall, too, right?

207
00:15:12,180 --> 00:15:12,960
That's right.

208
00:15:13,610 --> 00:15:14,790
Take him along with you, son.

209
00:15:14,810 --> 00:15:17,220
He's already packed all his stuff.

210
00:15:17,240 --> 00:15:18,020
Right, Cupid?

211
00:15:19,490 --> 00:15:20,370
Yes, My Lady.

212
00:15:20,930 --> 00:15:21,900
Khaomao, Khaopuk!

213
00:15:22,350 --> 00:15:23,870
- Yes? Yes!
- Yes.

214
00:15:28,120 --> 00:15:29,600
What about you, Belle?

215
00:15:29,640 --> 00:15:31,710
Do you have anywhere else
you want to go?

216
00:15:31,740 --> 00:15:34,480
Or are you moving somewhere soon?

217
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:37,250
I mean, how much longer
are you planning to stay here?

218
00:15:38,040 --> 00:15:40,470
That would depend on Thear.

219
00:15:42,330 --> 00:15:44,200
Where do you want her to move to?

220
00:15:44,670 --> 00:15:46,780
I asked her to come stay with me.

221
00:15:46,800 --> 00:15:48,240
She's staying for the long haul.

222
00:15:48,270 --> 00:15:49,840
It'll be easier for me
to take care of her.

223
00:15:52,510 --> 00:15:56,200
You take such good care of your friend,
don't you?

224
00:15:56,720 --> 00:15:59,240
But you're terrible
at taking care of your husband.

225
00:15:59,590 --> 00:16:01,450
Aren't you doing a pretty bad job here?

226
00:16:05,850 --> 00:16:10,420
Have you had
any aches or pains, Mungkorn?

227
00:16:11,630 --> 00:16:12,600
No.

228
00:16:15,780 --> 00:16:16,820
That's good.

229
00:16:17,540 --> 00:16:20,860
That proves I've been
taking pretty good care of him, Mom.

230
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:25,500
Is everything ready, Cupid?

231
00:16:25,610 --> 00:16:26,630
I'm tired of waiting.

232
00:16:26,830 --> 00:16:29,170
- Khaomao, Khaopuk, hurry up!
- Coming.

233
00:16:30,020 --> 00:16:31,880
Wait, where's Puk? Puk, move it!

234
00:16:32,010 --> 00:16:33,020
Gosh.

235
00:16:33,270 --> 00:16:35,220
You're so slow.
Keep those feet moving fast.

236
00:16:35,250 --> 00:16:37,480
- Hurry.
- It's so heavy. What's even in here?

237
00:16:39,240 --> 00:16:40,280
Here it is.

238
00:16:43,130 --> 00:16:44,980
- Ready for you to be Mowgli now.
- Right.

239
00:16:48,640 --> 00:16:49,620
Let me help you with your bag.

240
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:52,820
Let's go.

241
00:16:53,630 --> 00:16:54,420
Bye, Mom.

242
00:16:54,630 --> 00:16:55,820
Have a great trip.

243
00:16:57,270 --> 00:16:58,550
What do we do now?

244
00:16:59,760 --> 00:17:01,380
Yes, My Lady. Let's go.

245
00:17:01,990 --> 00:17:03,350
Go. Hurry up.

246
00:17:07,530 --> 00:17:08,550
Lady Pharada,

247
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:10,460
I think I'd better not go.

248
00:17:11,070 --> 00:17:12,610
It'll just be awkward for everyone.

249
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:13,700
You must go, dear.

250
00:17:13,920 --> 00:17:15,610
I've already paved the way for you.

251
00:17:17,660 --> 00:17:22,550
This is what I want to entrust to you
before I'm gone.

252
00:17:23,970 --> 00:17:26,250
You absolutely cannot give up, Mungkorn.

253
00:17:26,520 --> 00:17:27,580
Are you dying?

254
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:28,520
I'm going on a trip.

255
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:32,140
I have a trip
with the other police wives.

256
00:17:51,730 --> 00:17:53,420
Mungkorn, is there a song
you'd like to hear?

257
00:17:54,600 --> 00:17:56,060
I'm fine with anything.

258
00:17:59,300 --> 00:18:01,160
Then let's go with this one.

259
00:18:10,920 --> 00:18:15,720
♪I have a heart to give,
when will you receive it?♪

260
00:18:16,940 --> 00:18:22,080
♪Can you hear it?
My love, can you hear my wishes?♪

261
00:18:22,740 --> 00:18:26,010
♪All of my heart...♪

262
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:26,720
Hey.

263
00:18:27,260 --> 00:18:29,600
Why? Don't you like this song?

264
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:32,690
It's not that.

265
00:18:33,260 --> 00:18:35,190
I don't like listening to music
while driving anymore.

266
00:18:35,450 --> 00:18:36,640
It's distracting.

267
00:18:47,620 --> 00:18:49,950
I'm sorry, Belle,
for having to tag along.

268
00:18:51,190 --> 00:18:52,930
Lady Pharada forced me to come.

269
00:18:53,960 --> 00:18:56,760
It's totally fine.
The more, the merrier.

270
00:18:57,350 --> 00:19:00,150
She probably wanted you and Thear
to spend some time together.

271
00:19:00,550 --> 00:19:02,850
If anything, I'm the third wheel here.

272
00:19:03,530 --> 00:19:04,600
No, you're not.

273
00:19:04,810 --> 00:19:07,510
I wanted to come with you anyway.

274
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:15,340
Honestly, I don't think
marriage can change one's luck,

275
00:19:16,040 --> 00:19:18,980
but I understand that Thear
wanted to put his mom's mind at ease.

276
00:19:21,360 --> 00:19:22,500
You don't have to worry.

277
00:19:22,850 --> 00:19:25,440
It'll be six months before you know it.

278
00:19:25,870 --> 00:19:28,600
By the time you're back next time,
I'll be single again.

279
00:19:30,700 --> 00:19:32,030
Why are you telling me this?

280
00:19:32,850 --> 00:19:34,220
You should care about Mungkorn, too.

281
00:19:34,250 --> 00:19:36,820
He's helped you so much,
yet you're still being mean to him.

282
00:19:38,240 --> 00:19:39,310
How so?

283
00:19:39,940 --> 00:19:40,810
Ask him yourself.

284
00:19:41,010 --> 00:19:42,740
He's benefiting from this marriage, too.

285
00:19:43,460 --> 00:19:44,260
That's right.

286
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:47,590
I'm doing this only for the benefits.

287
00:19:49,280 --> 00:19:50,560
Once he's free of me,

288
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:54,130
he can go back to being a playboy
just like before.

289
00:20:11,970 --> 00:20:13,580
Is your bag heavy? Want me to carry it?

290
00:20:14,040 --> 00:20:15,900
It's not. I can carry it.

291
00:20:19,960 --> 00:20:21,100
Careful, it's slippery.

292
00:20:23,340 --> 00:20:24,860
Let me lead the way.

293
00:20:27,780 --> 00:20:29,050
Come on, hold onto me.

294
00:20:29,450 --> 00:20:31,130
I'm fine. I can manage. Look.

295
00:20:31,570 --> 00:20:34,370
Come on, just listen to me.
You might fall and hurt yourself.

296
00:20:34,910 --> 00:20:36,520
You don't need to fuss over me.

297
00:20:36,840 --> 00:20:37,960
I can take care of myself.

298
00:20:38,340 --> 00:20:39,270
I can't help it.

299
00:20:39,420 --> 00:20:41,510
I want you to know
that I've never changed.

300
00:20:41,540 --> 00:20:44,090
When I love someone,
I always take the best care of them.

301
00:20:44,340 --> 00:20:45,350
It's okay.

302
00:20:45,520 --> 00:20:48,100
I'm a modern woman.
I can handle myself just fine.

303
00:20:48,240 --> 00:20:48,960
Look.

304
00:20:49,970 --> 00:20:51,220
Come on, it's dangerous.

305
00:20:51,240 --> 00:20:52,320
See?

306
00:20:54,020 --> 00:20:55,180
Careful.

307
00:20:55,210 --> 00:20:55,950
Okay.

308
00:21:24,260 --> 00:21:25,060
Are you okay?

309
00:21:25,900 --> 00:21:26,920
I'm fine.

310
00:21:27,280 --> 00:21:28,160
Thanks.

311
00:21:29,130 --> 00:21:30,430
Watch your step, will you?

312
00:21:30,780 --> 00:21:32,760
If you fall,
you might end up with amnesia.

313
00:21:33,300 --> 00:21:34,440
That might actually be good.

314
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:36,600
There are things
I'd like to forget anyway.

315
00:21:41,060 --> 00:21:41,930
Wow.

316
00:21:42,080 --> 00:21:43,980
The water is so clear.
It makes me wanna jump right in,

317
00:21:44,340 --> 00:21:46,470
but I'm not going to swim today.

318
00:21:46,600 --> 00:21:48,380
Why? We're already here.

319
00:21:49,240 --> 00:21:51,160
I'm on my period.
It's the first day.

320
00:21:51,750 --> 00:21:53,260
You and Mungkorn go ahead and swim.

321
00:21:53,290 --> 00:21:54,720
I'll cheer you on from up here.

322
00:21:57,630 --> 00:22:00,220
If you're not going to swim,
I'm not going to swim.

323
00:22:00,640 --> 00:22:02,190
Would you let Mungkorn swim alone, then?

324
00:22:02,530 --> 00:22:03,490
It's okay.

325
00:22:03,960 --> 00:22:05,470
No need to bother him.

326
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:10,120
Let's hurry up
and put our things away

327
00:22:10,450 --> 00:22:11,660
so we can finally have fun.

328
00:22:46,530 --> 00:22:47,250
Hey!

329
00:22:47,570 --> 00:22:48,040
Belle!

330
00:22:48,060 --> 00:22:49,510
Whoa, it got in my ear.

331
00:22:49,640 --> 00:22:52,070
You're going for it
'cause I can't pull you down, huh?

332
00:22:53,150 --> 00:22:54,830
Take that.

333
00:22:54,850 --> 00:22:57,420
Mungkorn, help me.
This guy needs to be taught a lesson.

334
00:22:57,440 --> 00:23:00,040
You're so mean, huh?

335
00:23:00,490 --> 00:23:01,720
Fine. You want this?

336
00:23:04,010 --> 00:23:05,260
Come on, Mungkorn.

337
00:23:07,980 --> 00:23:08,870
Whoa!

338
00:23:10,070 --> 00:23:10,870
Hey!

339
00:23:13,050 --> 00:23:14,170
Whoa, wait.

340
00:23:15,530 --> 00:23:16,690
Isn't that too much?

341
00:23:16,990 --> 00:23:18,280
I can even give you more than that.

342
00:23:19,170 --> 00:23:19,880
Hey!

343
00:23:19,960 --> 00:23:20,590
Whoa.

344
00:23:21,270 --> 00:23:22,260
Are you holding a grudge?

345
00:23:23,280 --> 00:23:25,040
Don't make this personal.

346
00:23:25,870 --> 00:23:27,740
Want me to dunk you, then?

347
00:23:31,820 --> 00:23:33,460
You can't beat me. Come on.

348
00:23:34,220 --> 00:23:35,180
- Bring it on.
- Bring it on.

349
00:23:35,570 --> 00:23:36,400
Come on.

350
00:23:42,670 --> 00:23:43,630
Stop it.

351
00:23:48,120 --> 00:23:49,910
I don't think this is going to work.

352
00:23:50,190 --> 00:23:51,970
Having me play the evil ex

353
00:23:51,990 --> 00:23:53,770
just to stop Mungkorn's bad luck?

354
00:23:53,830 --> 00:23:55,020
I can't bring myself to do it.

355
00:23:55,210 --> 00:23:57,080
He's been so good to you.

356
00:24:01,230 --> 00:24:02,230
Ugh, I don't care.

357
00:24:02,250 --> 00:24:04,730
No matter what,
I have to make him hate me

358
00:24:04,750 --> 00:24:07,650
so I can take all that bad luck
back onto myself.

359
00:24:07,800 --> 00:24:10,800
Sure, Mr. Hero,
sacrificing everything for love.

360
00:24:11,220 --> 00:24:13,080
We never know when our time is up.

361
00:24:13,110 --> 00:24:15,020
We deserve to be
with the person we love.

362
00:24:18,540 --> 00:24:20,780
Otherwise, just get a divorce
and end this

363
00:24:21,520 --> 00:24:23,010
because what you're doing

364
00:24:23,240 --> 00:24:24,940
makes it seem like
you don't care about him at all.

365
00:24:26,800 --> 00:24:28,130
Yeah, I just...

366
00:24:29,630 --> 00:24:32,060
I just want to stay with him
a little longer.

367
00:24:34,110 --> 00:24:36,020
Whatever, I don't buy it.

368
00:24:36,670 --> 00:24:39,360
And you shouldn't let an oracle
dictate your life.

369
00:24:39,380 --> 00:24:42,280
I saw him get shot
right before my eyes, Belle.

370
00:24:42,470 --> 00:24:44,350
I didn't believe it at first,

371
00:24:45,240 --> 00:24:46,910
but now I'd rather not take any chances.

372
00:24:47,290 --> 00:24:49,240
Please forgive her, Heaven and Earth.

373
00:24:55,490 --> 00:24:56,910
You love him a lot, don't you?

374
00:25:00,070 --> 00:25:00,950
Yeah.

375
00:25:01,150 --> 00:25:02,220
It's okay.

376
00:25:02,830 --> 00:25:05,880
I'll do whatever it takes
to help you through this.

377
00:25:09,000 --> 00:25:10,050
Thanks

378
00:25:11,090 --> 00:25:14,580
for always loving and caring about me.

379
00:25:33,360 --> 00:25:34,800
You're jealous
of me and Belle, aren't you?

380
00:25:35,270 --> 00:25:36,810
Don't flatter yourself.

381
00:25:37,240 --> 00:25:40,000
I'm just doing
what Lady Pharada asked me to do.

382
00:25:40,500 --> 00:25:41,580
Don't lose your focus.

383
00:25:42,500 --> 00:25:43,900
It's only six more months.

384
00:25:44,380 --> 00:25:45,500
Is it that unbearable?

385
00:25:47,500 --> 00:25:48,300
That's right.

386
00:25:48,860 --> 00:25:49,940
It is unbearable.

387
00:25:50,250 --> 00:25:52,300
I can't wait to put an end to this.

388
00:25:53,390 --> 00:25:55,030
Then just let me go.

389
00:25:59,060 --> 00:25:59,940
Let go of me.

390
00:26:03,600 --> 00:26:04,680
Inspector...

391
00:26:05,270 --> 00:26:06,260
Let me go.

392
00:26:06,410 --> 00:26:07,280
Let go!

393
00:26:09,960 --> 00:26:10,830
Belle?

394
00:26:11,810 --> 00:26:12,780
Where is she?

395
00:26:13,460 --> 00:26:14,590
Hey, Belle.

396
00:26:17,450 --> 00:26:18,930
I'd better go call her.

397
00:26:21,060 --> 00:26:21,810
Belle!

398
00:26:26,740 --> 00:26:29,440
(I'm having cramps, so I'm leaving.
I'll pick you up tomorrow.)

399
00:26:30,070 --> 00:26:31,500
Wow, Belle.

400
00:26:53,890 --> 00:26:54,690
What are you doing?

401
00:26:56,480 --> 00:26:57,700
Setting up my tent, obviously.

402
00:27:05,760 --> 00:27:06,910
No need for that.

403
00:27:09,090 --> 00:27:10,340
We'll just sleep in the same one.

404
00:27:10,550 --> 00:27:12,080
So you wanna sleep next to me now?

405
00:27:13,710 --> 00:27:15,450
You were disgusted with me last night.

406
00:27:16,300 --> 00:27:17,430
I wasn't.

407
00:27:18,830 --> 00:27:20,100
I was just confused.

408
00:27:20,910 --> 00:27:21,910
Confused about what?

409
00:27:26,920 --> 00:27:28,620
Confused about...

410
00:27:29,870 --> 00:27:31,930
how I should treat you.

411
00:27:36,360 --> 00:27:37,560
I was feeling bad for Belle.

412
00:27:42,090 --> 00:27:43,050
Okay.

413
00:27:44,380 --> 00:27:46,610
In that case,
I'll clear up your confusion for you.

414
00:27:54,540 --> 00:27:55,260
Wait.

415
00:27:57,210 --> 00:27:58,150
Where are you going?

416
00:27:58,760 --> 00:28:00,540
To ask the staff to take me home.

417
00:28:02,800 --> 00:28:03,690
Don't do that.

418
00:28:06,200 --> 00:28:07,620
Can you stay with me tonight?

419
00:28:13,230 --> 00:28:14,460
Why would I?

420
00:28:15,570 --> 00:28:16,980
In fact,

421
00:28:17,950 --> 00:28:19,390
I wasn't even supposed to be here.

422
00:28:24,560 --> 00:28:25,740
Things have changed.

423
00:28:50,930 --> 00:28:51,900
Want a beer?

424
00:29:03,110 --> 00:29:04,430
Do you remember these mugs?

425
00:29:05,020 --> 00:29:06,580
I'm still using them, you know.

426
00:29:18,020 --> 00:29:19,320
I'll do it myself.

427
00:29:27,730 --> 00:29:28,910
Have you put it on yet?

428
00:29:33,830 --> 00:29:34,400
Here.

429
00:29:43,900 --> 00:29:45,300
It's okay. I'll do it myself.

430
00:30:03,200 --> 00:30:05,030
Can I ask you something, Inspector?

431
00:30:11,170 --> 00:30:13,170
Belle is such a lovely person.

432
00:30:15,380 --> 00:30:18,440
How could you let her
slip through your fingers?

433
00:30:21,770 --> 00:30:24,330
It's because of
my cunning, playboy ways.

434
00:30:27,020 --> 00:30:28,880
By the time I was ready to change,
it was too late.

435
00:30:31,460 --> 00:30:32,820
What if she...

436
00:30:34,030 --> 00:30:36,300
gave you a chance?

437
00:30:37,820 --> 00:30:39,410
Would you do it for her?

438
00:30:44,610 --> 00:30:45,410
I don't know.

439
00:30:48,290 --> 00:30:49,520
Someone like me...

440
00:30:50,150 --> 00:30:52,850
probably deserves
to be punished by fate

441
00:30:54,400 --> 00:30:56,080
and be alone for the rest of my life.

442
00:30:58,220 --> 00:31:00,200
Whoever I love,
I just bring them bad luck

443
00:31:01,540 --> 00:31:02,950
and end up breaking their heart.

444
00:31:08,540 --> 00:31:09,790
You've only got yourself to blame.

445
00:31:16,180 --> 00:31:17,540
I think...

446
00:31:19,840 --> 00:31:21,840
there's always a chance to do better.

447
00:31:23,460 --> 00:31:25,930
Why keep making the same old mistakes?

448
00:31:27,470 --> 00:31:29,500
If you just change and become a new man,

449
00:31:30,390 --> 00:31:32,550
I'm sure Belle could fall for you again.

450
00:31:48,800 --> 00:31:50,600
But I don't want Belle
to fall for me again.

451
00:32:13,100 --> 00:32:14,310
I'm going to the bathroom.

452
00:32:38,950 --> 00:32:39,830
Mungkorn.

453
00:32:40,500 --> 00:32:43,000
Why are you doing it here?
Why don't you use the bathroom?

454
00:32:43,030 --> 00:32:44,420
Something might snatch you up.

455
00:32:44,630 --> 00:32:45,720
There's nothing out here.

456
00:32:46,470 --> 00:32:47,570
Why did you follow me?

457
00:32:47,590 --> 00:32:50,760
I'm worried about you.
What if a tiger takes you?

458
00:32:51,360 --> 00:32:52,720
There are no tigers here.

459
00:32:53,430 --> 00:32:54,700
This isn't their hunting ground.

460
00:33:03,810 --> 00:33:05,250
Sh*t! A snake!

461
00:33:06,060 --> 00:33:06,820
Hey, wait.

462
00:33:06,840 --> 00:33:07,750
Right there!

463
00:33:07,780 --> 00:33:09,750
- It really is a snake.
- Yeah, I told you! Go!

464
00:33:09,850 --> 00:33:11,440
Go, Mungkorn!

465
00:33:11,460 --> 00:33:13,690
Is it gone? Move over here.

466
00:33:13,710 --> 00:33:14,820
Are there any more?

467
00:33:14,850 --> 00:33:17,760
It's gone, Inspector.
It went over there.

468
00:33:18,320 --> 00:33:19,400
Jeez...

469
00:33:21,300 --> 00:33:22,800
My legs are covered in pee now.

470
00:33:31,950 --> 00:33:32,770
Just a stick.

471
00:33:37,040 --> 00:33:38,100
For an inspector,

472
00:33:39,040 --> 00:33:40,140
you're terrified of snakes, huh?

473
00:33:40,170 --> 00:33:41,380
What does my rank have to do with it?

474
00:33:41,400 --> 00:33:43,520
I just don't like them.
They're gross and slimy.

475
00:33:45,520 --> 00:33:47,360
How are you so calm?

476
00:33:47,530 --> 00:33:49,370
Snakes get into my house all the time.

477
00:33:49,400 --> 00:33:50,430
It's nothing new to me.

478
00:33:51,430 --> 00:33:52,930
I could even catch one to show you.

479
00:33:52,960 --> 00:33:54,670
No need to go that far.

480
00:33:56,980 --> 00:33:59,090
Don't tell anyone about this, okay?

481
00:34:00,030 --> 00:34:01,150
It's embarrassing.

482
00:34:01,930 --> 00:34:03,450
Nobody else knows about this.

483
00:34:04,910 --> 00:34:06,430
I won't tell a soul, Inspector.

484
00:34:07,330 --> 00:34:10,140
I'm great at keeping secrets,
you know that.

485
00:34:16,180 --> 00:34:17,230
Can we go now?

486
00:34:18,670 --> 00:34:21,490
It's coming back!

487
00:34:21,510 --> 00:34:22,890
What is wrong with you?

488
00:34:23,260 --> 00:34:24,720
I'm heading into the tent.

489
00:34:25,260 --> 00:34:26,340
It's just a stick.

490
00:34:40,690 --> 00:34:42,120
Calm down, Inspector.

491
00:34:57,520 --> 00:34:58,520
I've already checked.

492
00:34:59,120 --> 00:35:00,290
No snakes around here.

493
00:35:02,720 --> 00:35:03,620
Thanks a lot.

494
00:35:06,020 --> 00:35:07,060
You should get some sleep

495
00:35:07,810 --> 00:35:09,040
so we can leave early.

496
00:35:11,730 --> 00:35:12,980
You're the only one

497
00:35:13,740 --> 00:35:15,590
who gets to see this side of me.

498
00:35:17,870 --> 00:35:20,170
Even Belle has never seen you like this?

499
00:35:21,120 --> 00:35:21,880
Never.

500
00:35:22,460 --> 00:35:23,760
I can't let anyone else see it.

501
00:35:24,370 --> 00:35:26,380
I'm supposed to be the cool inspector.

502
00:35:26,560 --> 00:35:27,960
I'm not allowed to be afraid.

503
00:35:28,270 --> 00:35:30,220
Always have to be the protector.

504
00:35:31,520 --> 00:35:32,980
But since you came along,

505
00:35:33,860 --> 00:35:35,850
I can let my guard down.

506
00:35:38,770 --> 00:35:41,560
Do you really have to
put on an act like that?

507
00:35:43,310 --> 00:35:44,300
Doesn't it get exhausting?

508
00:35:45,910 --> 00:35:47,420
When you love someone,

509
00:35:47,790 --> 00:35:49,900
you should be able to be yourself.

510
00:35:56,720 --> 00:35:57,760
I'm heading to bed.

511
00:36:16,430 --> 00:36:18,060
I'm sorry for making you upset,

512
00:36:18,990 --> 00:36:20,370
but it was necessary.

513
00:36:35,520 --> 00:36:36,990
I think I understand.

514
00:36:40,200 --> 00:36:41,930
It's just that the timing...

515
00:36:43,010 --> 00:36:44,220
is all wrong.

516
00:36:45,900 --> 00:36:47,350
If it weren't for me,

517
00:36:49,140 --> 00:36:51,880
you and Belle
would've gotten back together by now.

518
00:36:58,030 --> 00:37:00,030
Should I explain things to Lady Pharada?

519
00:37:02,060 --> 00:37:03,240
I'm sure she would understand.

520
00:37:08,550 --> 00:37:09,950
Or maybe...

521
00:37:12,220 --> 00:37:14,120
your bad luck
has finally run its course.

522
00:37:14,150 --> 00:37:15,420
It hasn't!

523
00:37:17,630 --> 00:37:20,050
(But why is it Mungkorn
who's having all the bad luck instead?)

524
00:37:20,080 --> 00:37:23,270
I told you already.
You are meant to live as one.

525
00:37:23,290 --> 00:37:26,260
Yet you have heeded none of my words.

526
00:37:26,290 --> 00:37:28,720
The heaven and earth
do not acknowledge your love.

527
00:37:31,980 --> 00:37:32,690
Here goes.

528
00:37:33,370 --> 00:37:36,520
Please, Heaven and Earth,
and the spirits of the forest, help me.

529
00:37:36,620 --> 00:37:38,210
It probably won't be what I'm thinking.

530
00:37:39,940 --> 00:37:40,990
What exactly are you thinking?

531
00:37:50,780 --> 00:37:52,360
Wait, Inspector.

532
00:37:52,910 --> 00:37:54,360
No more waiting.

533
00:37:54,380 --> 00:37:56,820
Please just let me
be a good husband for once.

534
00:39:50,100 --> 00:39:51,630
If I'd known it would be this good,

535
00:39:52,720 --> 00:39:55,750
I would've let you do it
from the day we got married.

536
00:39:58,970 --> 00:40:00,270
Was it really that good?

537
00:40:02,690 --> 00:40:04,680
It was exactly like Lukplub told me.

538
00:40:06,030 --> 00:40:07,920
He said it'd feel so warm...

539
00:40:08,820 --> 00:40:10,960
like being showered with love
from the whole world.

540
00:40:14,390 --> 00:40:15,700
You don't need the whole world.

541
00:40:16,370 --> 00:40:19,220
Just me alone is more than enough.

542
00:40:26,710 --> 00:40:28,090
I'm really happy...

543
00:40:29,140 --> 00:40:30,510
that my first time...

544
00:40:31,570 --> 00:40:34,210
happened when we actually
had feelings for each other.

545
00:40:44,310 --> 00:40:45,630
Right, Thear?

546
00:40:48,720 --> 00:40:50,590
We did it out of love, didn't we?

547
00:40:54,010 --> 00:40:54,840
Of course we did.

548
00:40:57,300 --> 00:40:58,820
Everything that happened...

549
00:40:59,400 --> 00:41:00,770
and every single touch...

550
00:41:01,600 --> 00:41:03,320
came from love.

551
00:41:20,830 --> 00:41:24,710
Then let's do
another couple activity, shall we?

552
00:41:26,510 --> 00:41:27,480
What now?

553
00:41:38,650 --> 00:41:39,800
Face masks.

554
00:41:43,260 --> 00:41:44,700
Wow, you're really well-prepared.

555
00:41:54,840 --> 00:41:55,830
Part your hair.

556
00:42:36,120 --> 00:42:37,570
Well, it feels cool.

557
00:42:38,270 --> 00:42:39,270
Does it feel refreshing?

558
00:42:39,990 --> 00:42:40,930
It does.

559
00:42:48,270 --> 00:42:49,180
What are you doing?

560
00:42:49,210 --> 00:42:50,870
Setting a timer for 15 minutes.

561
00:42:54,350 --> 00:42:55,280
Okay.

562
00:43:53,290 --> 00:43:54,520
Is it morning already?

563
00:43:56,310 --> 00:43:58,340
I slept so well
that I completely overslept.

564
00:44:01,340 --> 00:44:02,520
You can sleep a bit longer.

565
00:44:03,660 --> 00:44:05,190
The weather's nice and warm.

566
00:44:05,790 --> 00:44:06,890
It's perfect for cuddling.

567
00:44:10,140 --> 00:44:11,830
Should we stay another night?

568
00:44:13,690 --> 00:44:17,260
I don't think anything else will happen.

569
00:44:18,100 --> 00:44:19,490
Anything else?

570
00:44:20,380 --> 00:44:21,470
What do you mean?

571
00:44:23,640 --> 00:44:25,170
Oh, I just mean...

572
00:44:25,520 --> 00:44:27,910
there shouldn't be
anything to worry about

573
00:44:28,170 --> 00:44:29,860
or get in our way,

574
00:44:30,270 --> 00:44:31,500
like wild animals.

575
00:44:31,700 --> 00:44:33,690
Tigers or snakes, you know.

576
00:44:34,370 --> 00:44:35,420
No more.

577
00:44:36,890 --> 00:44:39,350
Just some wolf-manizer around here.

578
00:44:42,190 --> 00:44:44,410
Wanna see what this wolf can do
in the morning?

579
00:44:44,930 --> 00:44:45,680
I can do this.

580
00:44:46,170 --> 00:44:47,020
And this.

581
00:44:47,040 --> 00:44:48,020
Stop it.

582
00:44:48,040 --> 00:44:49,140
You're not actually a wolf.

583
00:44:50,150 --> 00:44:51,100
I'm a wolf snake.

584
00:44:51,520 --> 00:44:52,530
That's a venomous snake.

585
00:44:52,550 --> 00:44:53,450
No, it's not.

586
00:44:55,360 --> 00:44:56,180
But you are.

587
00:44:56,370 --> 00:44:57,890
Good morning!

588
00:44:57,940 --> 00:44:58,890
Whoa, Belle!

589
00:44:59,290 --> 00:45:00,620
- Belle, can you give us a minute?
- Belle...

590
00:45:01,630 --> 00:45:02,560
We'll be right out.

591
00:45:03,490 --> 00:45:04,740
My bad. I'm sorry.

592
00:45:04,900 --> 00:45:06,190
I didn't think you'd go this far.

593
00:45:32,160 --> 00:45:33,560
So, everything's settled?

594
00:45:35,530 --> 00:45:36,300
Well...

595
00:45:38,200 --> 00:45:39,130
It's just as it looks.

596
00:45:40,910 --> 00:45:44,710
I told you. We are the ones
who decide our own fate.

597
00:45:47,350 --> 00:45:49,260
The weather's so refreshing today.

598
00:45:51,240 --> 00:45:53,810
Heaven and earth are on our side.

599
00:46:03,610 --> 00:46:04,860
Hey, Mungkorn!

600
00:46:12,020 --> 00:46:13,160
Are you hurt? Did it hit you?

601
00:46:14,070 --> 00:46:14,950
I'm okay.

602
00:46:15,540 --> 00:46:16,960
Whoa, that was a close call.

603
00:46:29,460 --> 00:46:30,200
Where are you going?

604
00:46:30,230 --> 00:46:32,900
To help Captain arrest the Black Bull
at the karaoke bar.

605
00:46:32,930 --> 00:46:33,690
You can't go.

606
00:46:33,820 --> 00:46:35,260
When I give you an order,
you follow it.

607
00:46:35,280 --> 00:46:36,430
I'm your superior.

608
00:46:36,650 --> 00:46:38,120
I really don't know my place.

609
00:46:38,150 --> 00:46:40,850
I know full well
I'm just meant to ward off his bad luck.

610
00:46:40,910 --> 00:46:42,000
A guy like that

611
00:46:42,030 --> 00:46:43,560
isn't worth your love.

612
00:46:43,720 --> 00:46:45,310
You deserve someone better.

613
00:46:45,340 --> 00:46:46,240
If it were me,

614
00:46:46,260 --> 00:46:48,030
I would never hurt you.

615
00:46:48,050 --> 00:46:49,360
So, you just wanted to sleep with me?

616
00:46:52,410 --> 00:46:57,290
♪Trying so hard not to cross the line,♪

617
00:46:57,320 --> 00:47:02,150
♪But the more I run,
the more you're on my mind♪

618
00:47:02,170 --> 00:47:06,440
♪If you're gonna love me,
don't break the deal we made♪

619
00:47:06,470 --> 00:47:11,930
♪Don't break my heart,
remember what you said?♪

620
00:47:11,950 --> 00:47:16,960
♪Let's call off the deal
and let our hearts decide♪

621
00:47:16,990 --> 00:47:23,360
♪From contracting parties to lovers,
does that sound alright?♪

622
00:47:29,690 --> 00:47:32,860
♪It's time you became mine♪
